WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
- They put the
protestors in buses.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
It started off with
400, then it was 1200.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.172
The last number I heard
was that they captured

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.375
about 1700 people
and they bring them

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the federal police
training facility in Brasilia,

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:15.348
stick 'em in the gymnasium. No
food, no water, no bathrooms.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.716
Young kids, no food.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.985
Old women, dehydrated.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
Intel says, and it's been
pretty well verified,

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.624 align:start size:88% position:13%
that at least one
person's died that day.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.859
I heard two people.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.128
Now they say it's
up to four or five.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.629 align:start size:81% position:19%
And they basically
create a gulag,

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.766
which are being called in
Brazil Lulacs: Lula gulags.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.034 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yeah.
- A portmanteau.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.903
And now, after two days of that,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.671
that was Monday and Tuesday,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.907
they let the women
and children go...

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.076 align:start size:84% position:16%
By the way, the
images of old people

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.544
sitting in puddles
of their own urine

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.779
because there's no bathrooms,

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:48.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
sweltering conditions,
no food, no water.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:52.819 align:start size:97% position:3%
They let the older women and
the women and children go

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.854
on the condition, and we
have these floating around,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.423
a denunciation page.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.591 align:start size:84% position:16%
You have to sign it
to be released saying,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:01.394
"I am a terrorist. I
assaulted democracy."

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.296
And this now has them on lists.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.998
They will never get a job again.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:08.068
(upbeat intro music)

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm Dave Rubin, and joining
me today is a journalist,

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.976
an author, and a Lincoln Fellow

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start size:97% position:3%
at the Claremont
Institute, Matthew Tyrmand.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.415 align:start size:97% position:3%
Matthew, finally welcome to
The Rubin Report. How are you?

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.817
- It's an honor to
be with you, Dave.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:97% position:3%
You forgot the most
important honorific: friend.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.755
- And friend.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:31.691
You are one of the people in
our little Florida crew here,

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.727
our little Florida Freedom crew.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.229
Basically, this is home base

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.898
for sanity throughout the world.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.101
I've wanted to have you
on for quite some time,

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know, there's
this whole thing...

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.537
Well, I know you know this.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.439
There is this whole
situation, let's say,

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:88% position:13%
happening in Brazil,
which has been unfolding

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.111
after these elections for
the last couple months.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.412
I've only talked about it

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:55.281
maybe two or three
times on the show.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.218
It is not my area of expertise,

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:84% position:16%
but the crazier it
seems to get out there

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:03.123 align:start position:0%
with the visuals of the
protestors and everything else,

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.892 align:start position:0%
it seems to me the more the
mainstream media is ignoring it

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.127
and that's one of the things

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.695
that always lights
up in my mind, like,

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.530 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Oh, mainstream
media's ignoring it.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.599
We better pay attention to it."

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.602
You basically have
been, I don't know,

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.770
possibly the most
outspoken person

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:21.241
from an American perspective
on what's going on in Brazil.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.675
So let's do this.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you give me 30 seconds
on your background,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.579 align:start size:88% position:13%
why people should trust
you on this topic?

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.815
And then let's do
a little Brazil 101

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.183
and then get people
caught up to speed

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.652
on what's going on
over there right now.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.586
- Sure.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.021
As I said, great to be with you

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.023
and you know, thank
you from, you know,

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.958
on my behalf as well
as Brazilian's behalf,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.994
because they feel
very, very ignored

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.062 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I've become
somewhat of their voice,

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.899
sort of for the Western press
from a right wing perspective,

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.200
a Conservative perspective,

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.403
an honest perspective as
they've been totally...

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.971
Their voice has been negated

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.640 align:start size:81% position:19%
as their laws have
been abrogated.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I didn't expect
Brazil to be my beat.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.145 align:start position:0%
I'm an investigative journalist
and a political activist.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.080
I wear my politics on my
sleeve; everybody knows it.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.050
This is not, you know, my
vocation professionally,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.985 align:start size:84% position:16%
I do not make money
as an activist

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.288
or in campaigns
or in journalism,

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.889
I do it because of
the love of the game

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.025
and the belief in
truth to power.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.793
You know, we have mutual
friends like James O'Keefe,

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.528
I'm on the board
of Project Veritas,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.864
I help manage a group in Chicago

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
called Open the Books that
does forensic auditing

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.100
in the public sector,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.303
all things I believe are
important to, you know,

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:24.837
make a more honest society

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:28.741
because our society is as
broken as it's ever been.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.910 align:start size:84% position:16%
I did not expect
Brazil to be my beat.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.613
I've been covering a lot of
international geopolitics

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.914
from a European perspective.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.416
I'm a Polish dual citizen.

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:38.284 align:start size:88% position:13%
I live in Europe, a
good chunk of the time.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've certainly covered
Russia-Ukraine,

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.921
especially from the
Polish perspective,

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.090
given that they're sort
of in the line of fire.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, I cover the
Sovereigntist movements

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:49.529 align:start size:84% position:16%
in Europe, Westphalian
sovereignty as
expressed in politics,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether it's Poland or Hungary
or the right wing parties

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:55.034 align:start size:97% position:3%
in Sweden and Spain and
France and Germany, et cetera.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.337 align:start size:88% position:13%
I didn't expect to do
Brazil, but here we are.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:00.106
I went there for CPAC in
'21 with Jason Miller,

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start position:0%
gave a speech about exactly
this, honest media, free press,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.678
culture war and lo and behold,

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.146
as we were exiting the country,

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.483
we were detained by Alexandre
Moraes, the Supreme Court,

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.219 align:start size:88% position:13%
which we will speak
about, and interrogated

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:16.256
and asked to write down the
names of who we met with,

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
the politicians, the
activists, the journalists

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.927 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it had a very Stalinesque
feel to it, you know?

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:24.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Give us the next tranche
of our enemies list."

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.099 align:start size:84% position:16%
Of course, we did
not comply with that

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.801 align:start size:97% position:3%
and from that, I, you know,
germinated an interest.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:29.736 align:start size:84% position:16%
I wanted to understand
exactly what-

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.237
- Wait, wait, wait. Hold on.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.706
I gotta pause you there. You're
trying to leave a country...

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:34.974
- Yes.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.809
- They ask you for the
list, they detain you,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.578 align:start size:84% position:16%
you don't comply...
- Yes.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.146
- That's not an
easy thing to do.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.215
I think you glossed
over how that ended.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.285
- Well, they said we
were not under arrest.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:49.222
We were part of what they call
The Fake News Investigation,

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.723
and we'll talk about this.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:54.027
For years, the court and the
burgeoning judicial autocracy

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:57.530 align:start position:0%
had put every one of the
political enemies of the court,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.699
of the Lula camp into this box

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:03.569
of by being critical of the
court or any of the things

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
in government that was not
aligned with Bolsonaro,

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.274 align:start size:88% position:13%
they were assaulting
democratic institutions.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.943 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's the sort of
framework that they applied.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:13.212
And so they've had this
Fake News Investigation

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.848 align:start size:97% position:3%
that has given them the
pretext to censor journalists,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.918
arrest journalists, even
arrest sitting members

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.787
of the Lower House in Brazil.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.222 align:start size:88% position:13%
They put Daniel Silveira
under house arrest.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:26.059 align:start size:88% position:13%
A lot of ankle bracelets
rolling around there.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.261 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so I knew that
going in to some degree.

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.330 align:start size:84% position:16%
I got educated
more on the ground.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.365
Jason Miller and I, and
if people don't know,

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:35.201
this is Trump's sort of
campaign main comms guy,

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.469
very, very close to Trump,

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.838
very, very high profile
figure in his own right.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.374 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he was building out
GETTR at the time, still is,

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:44.344 align:start size:88% position:13%
an alternative to
Twitter that, you know,

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:47.113 align:start size:84% position:16%
is more egalitarian,
freedom oriented,

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.416
especially as Twitter was
a highly censored platform,

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.151
as we all know, as
I know you know.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.754
And so he was going to
talk about that at CPAC

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:57.023
and promote it and I was
talking about, you know,

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.758
Project Veritas and media.

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I organized... Because
I am quite friendly

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:02.662
over the years with
Eduardo Bolsonaro

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:04.397
and other members of
the Bolsonaro family,

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:06.966
I organized a meeting with
all of us and Jair Bolsonaro,

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.968 align:start size:84% position:16%
the sitting president
at the palace

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.938
and those pictures that
we posted went viral.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.906 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it turned out
that on the Sunday...

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.174
We were leaving on a Monday.

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:19.112
On the Sunday after
CPAC had concluded,

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:22.248
news stories broke in
the stenographer press,

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:24.283 align:start size:97% position:3%
the guild carrying
mainstream press of Brazil,

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:27.920
which actually makes CNN
here look downright honest.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.888 align:start size:81% position:19%
(Dave laughing)
I mean, these guys

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:30.156 align:start size:72% position:28%
were really...
- Wow, wow.

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:33.226
- ... really Pravda,
really propagandist.

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:35.261 align:start size:97% position:3%
Incidentally, not
surprisingly, they were also

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:38.097 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the payroll of the previous
regimes quite heavily.

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:41.067
State-owned enterprises were
funding much of their revenue,

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.969
advertising and whatever else.

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:44.704
So they reported on
the Sunday afternoon

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:46.339
before we were supposed to leave

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.708 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we'd been under
surveillance from
the moment we landed.

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.176
And I told Jason, you know,

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.411
I spent a lot of time in
Central and Eastern Europe,

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:52.912
post-communist nations.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.680 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've been tapped, I've been
surveilled, I've been watched,

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.850 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've been dragged into, you
know, kangaroo court hearings.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.018
None of this stuff surprises me.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.253
And I told him, and I said,

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.387
"You know, there's a good chance

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.089 align:start size:88% position:13%
we're gonna be detained
at the airport."

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.590 align:start size:88% position:13%
And he goes, "No,
you're being paranoid."

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.426
"I'm not being paranoid. I
think it'd be kind of great.

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:09.328 align:start size:88% position:13%
It would serve the
point quite perfectly."

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:12.598 align:start size:97% position:3%
I also have dual citizenship,
which is kind of helpful.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:13.833
And we were.

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:16.102
So we were leaving
on Monday to fly out

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.704
and before we can get to our
plane, they say, you know,

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:20.573
"Please come with us."

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:24.043
We had a traveling party
of four, Jason, myself,

00:07:24.043 --> 00:07:27.280 align:start size:84% position:16%
and two dual Brazilian
American citizens

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.650
that came with us and also
had been involved with CPAC

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.884
and they really...

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.853
Jason was the main one
they wanted to talk to,

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:36.622
and so they let us sit on
the plane for a little bit.

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:38.558
And three, four hours goes by,

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:41.594
lawyers are called, State
Department lawyers called,

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:44.297 align:start size:97% position:3%
they say, "Well, you're
screwed. Get another lawyer."

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:45.798
So they weren't very helpful.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:49.569
Eventually, Jason was able
to procure a good lawyer

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:53.172
through Brazilian contacts to
come and help extricate us.

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:54.707
But it became a big story.

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:57.176
When we were flying out
Politico, CNN, Forbes,

00:07:57.176 --> 00:08:00.046 align:start size:84% position:16%
Business Insider,
they all picked it up
about our detention.

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:01.314
But it was very,
very instructive

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.049
of how heavy handed they are.

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:04.750 align:start size:84% position:16%
Here we are, you
know, not Brazilians,

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.520 align:start size:88% position:13%
just coming in in a
constitutional republic,

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.255 align:start size:81% position:19%
we can come and
speak our ideas...

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:10.723
Well, or so we thought.

00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:13.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
Apparently not without
some sort of repercussion.

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:16.295
And they wanted to probe and
understand who we met with

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:18.030
to add to their enemies list.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.532
So from that moment
on, I just said,

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.267
"I'm gonna go deep. I'm
gonna talk to people.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:24.237
I'm gonna really understand
the history, how we got here,

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:26.606 align:start size:88% position:13%
the mechanisms of
power that are in place

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:29.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
and being utilized to
clamp down on opposition."

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:31.911
And I learned a lot in
the following months

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:34.113
and I published on it
ahead of the election

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:36.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I basically predicted
that this election

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:38.618 align:start size:97% position:3%
would be filled with, you
know, to use a generous term,

00:08:38.618 --> 00:08:40.286
anomalies, but this...

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even Tucker said it the
other night when I was on,

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.390
the fix was in. The
fix was in, you know?

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.692
The real genesis
of the fix being in

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.795 align:start size:88% position:13%
was this court subsuming
all these powers

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:52.832
that are generally broken down
in a constitutional republic.

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:53.833
They're very Bismarckian.

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.134
